WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:11.038
Every AI demo works. That's the problem. A demo is a magic trick — the same inputs, the same happy path, every time. Your customers never use the happy path.

00:11.038 --> 00:24.031
Here's why. A demo shows maybe five hand-picked cases. Production throws thousands of real ones at it — typos, edge cases, weird phrasings, angry users. The demo never saw any of them.

00:24.031 --> 00:37.255
So the failure is guaranteed. Not because the model is bad, but because the thing that breaks it was never in the demo. The gap between five cases and ten thousand is where every AI feature dies.

00:37.255 --> 00:43.467
The fix isn't a better demo. It's testing every path — before your customer finds the one that breaks.

00:43.467 --> 00:48.000
Stop trusting demos. Test everything. That's what I do — let's talk.

